  "root_sources": "Kṣīrasvāmin in his own entry gives initial ṣṭ in ṣṭyāyati beside styāyati. His citation for strī has ḍraṭ and local number 4.165. The same-number primary digital Uṇādi text has ḍaṭ. These are witnesses at the same address, not a closure of the separate 4.105 field. Maitreya prints styāyati and tiṣṭyāsati.",
  "nominal_scope": "The two compounds have strī as their inflecting feminine head. The 26-reading strī schedule, including the two optional accusatives, survives with both directly compared head-final controls. For the three t-bearing neuters use an a-stem whose last consonant r triggers ending ṇ. The Mādhavīya’s formal abstract and the dictionary-specific sense remain separately labelled.",
